83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Every error is hidden. Here line.split\(""\) raises ValueError: empty separator on every line, the bare except swallows it, and the office sees an empty report and Total 0 without any warning. It also catches Ctrl-C and real bugs, so wrong totals look like correct output.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [37]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (int\("1250.50"\) raises ValueError, so that bill is silently dropped and the total is understated. Using float\(\) instead would give rounding errors \(0.1 + 0.2 problem\); money needs Decimal. In my test the paise bills were lost and the total was 1260 instead of 3825.75.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [38]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Students whose bill failed are never listed. The warden cannot tell who was skipped, cannot correct the line and rerun, and a student may go uncharged or be charged wrongly; there is no audit trail.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [39]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (The handle stays open until the program ends. On Windows the open file stays locked, so the office cannot rename, move or edit it, and handles leak if the script runs for many files. If an error occurs, buffers and the lock are not released promptly.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [40]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Works only on that one PC, user and month. It breaks for November's file, on another computer or on Linux, and the backslashes are error-prone. The code cannot be reused or tested without editing it.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [41]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (The full text, and then the list created by split\(\), are held in memory. For 50,000 lines my test used 5.6 MB peak against 0.02 MB line by line; a file ten thousand times larger could exhaust RAM on a small office PC.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [42]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Each report = report + ... creates a new string and copies the old text, so time grows towards O\(n squared\) for big files \(CPython can optimise some cases but it is not guaranteed\). Also the "" between name and amount adds no space, so 'Bala1300' runs together. Use a list and "\\n".join\(\) or write line by line.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [43]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
