202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 41 0 R
/T (For 50,000 lines my version reads one line at a time, so memory stays tiny and constant \(measured 0.02 MB against 5.6 MB for read\(\)\), and with closes the file even if an error occurs. Money is held as Decimal, so paise are exact. Specific checks reject bad lines and record the line number and reason, so no bill vanishes silently and the office can correct and rerun. The file name is a parameter, so one function serves every month. Unexpected errors are not hidden, so real bugs surface immediately.)
/E (For 50,000 lines my version reads one line at a time, so memory stays tiny and constant \(measured 0.02 MB against 5.6 MB for read\(\)\), and with closes the file even if an error occurs. Money is held as Decimal, so paise are exact. Specific checks reject bad lines and record the line number and reason, so no bill vanishes silently and the office can correct and rerun. The file name is a parameter, so one function serves every month. Unexpected errors are not hidden, so real bugs surface immediately.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [93]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 41 0 R
/T (Time: both designs are O\(n\) for n lines \(more exactly O\(file size\)\): every character is read and every line parsed once. The measured times are close \(0.13, 0.15 and 0.17 s\) because most time is spent in Decimal parsing, not in reading. read\(\) plus split does one extra pass to cut lines. Memory: read\(\) holds the whole text, O\(file size\); readlines\(\) holds 50,000 separate string objects \(each has about 49 bytes of object overhead plus its characters\),)
/E (Time: both designs are O\(n\) for n lines \(more exactly O\(file size\)\): every character is read and every line parsed once. The measured times are close \(0.13, 0.15 and 0.17 s\) because most time is spent in Decimal parsing, not in reading. read\(\) plus split does one extra pass to cut lines. Memory: read\(\) holds the whole text, O\(file size\); readlines\(\) holds 50,000 separate string objects \(each has about 49 bytes of object overhead plus its characters\),)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [94]
>>
endobj
