/Title (For 50,000 lines my version reads one line at a time, so memory stays tiny and constant \(measured 0.02 MB against 5.6 MB for read\(\)\), and with closes the file even if an error occurs. Money is held as Decimal, so paise are exact. Specific checks reject bad lines and record the line number and reason, so no bill vanishes silently and the office can correct and rerun. The file name is a parameter, so one function serves every month. Unexpected errors are not hidden, so real bugs surface immediately.)
