537 0 obj
<<
/Title (Time: both designs are O\(n\) for n lines \(more exactly O\(file size\)\): every character is read and every line parsed once. The measured times are close \(0.13, 0.15 and 0.17 s\) because most time is spent in Decimal parsing, not in reading. read\(\) plus split does one extra pass to cut lines. Memory: read\(\) holds the whole text, O\(file size\); readlines\(\) holds 50,000 separate string objects \(each has about 49 bytes of object overhead plus its characters\),)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 451 0 R
/Prev 486 0 R
/Next 591 0 R
>>
