540 0 obj
<<
/Title (Extrapolating linearly, a file with 5 million lines would need about 400 to 560 MB with read\(\) or readlines\(\) but still about 0.02 MB with iteration. The alternative is acceptable only when the file is small or when the program needs random access to all lines \(for example sorting or a second pass\); otherwise line-by-line is the safer design.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 489 0 R
/Prev 539 0 R
>>
